    "result_text": "All 255 tests pass (including the new `AcceptanceTest`), BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI released version 2 of the owner identity. The change centers on a new **version-2 region code** \u2014 the plain region combined with a fixed `V2` tag \u2014 mixed *inside* the identifier derivations while the user-facing region stays plain.\n\n**Version-2 region code** (`PostcodeRegions`)\n- Added `regionCode(postcode)` (plain: `NSW`/`VIC`/`QLD`/`UNKNOWN`) and `regionCodeV2(postcode)` = `<region>-V2`.\n\n**Rederived identifiers** (all three now change, none reproduce a v1 value)\n- `AssignOwnerMemberId` \u2014 REGION prefix stays the *plain* region (so `locality` still parses it), but `HASH8` now hashes `regionCodeV2 | telephone | lastName`, so the memberId is rederived.\n- `AssignOwnerHousehold` \u2014 `householdId` now hashes `regionCodeV2 | lastName | postcode` (still a pure function of last name + postcode, so households still coalesce).\n- `OwnerIdentity.identityKey` \u2014 now hashes `regionCodeV2 | telephone | email | soundex(lastName)`; both sides of the duplicate check canonicalize identically, so 409 detection stays consistent.\n\n**V2 tag stays out of user-facing fields** \u2014 `locality`, `timezone` and `ownerSegment` all derive from the plain region (via the memberId's plain prefix), so the `V2` tag never surfaces there.\n\n**Response shape** (`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper`)\n- New `OwnerIdentity` schema; `memberId`/`householdId`/`identityKey` moved off the top level into a nested `identity` object.\n- Added top-level integer `apiVersion: 2`.\n\n**Audit** (`AuditOwnerCreated`)\n- Structured event moved to schema version 2: added `schemaVersion: 2` and an `ownerSegment` recomputed from the version-2 identity.\n\nRequest fields (`OwnerFields`) are unchanged.\n\nThe new acceptance test confirms the contract: `apiVersion == 2`, `identity.{memberId,identityKey,householdId}` present, and those three no longer exist at the top level.",
