    "probe_text": "I've now read the entire pipeline (`api/owners.POST.yml`) and every function class it references, plus the bean-validation constraints on the request DTO. Here is everything that happens, in execution order.\n\n## Endpoint guard (before the pipeline)\n- **[validation] Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. Without that role the request is rejected (403) before any step runs.\n\n## Pipeline steps (in order)\n\n**1. `checkIdempotency` \u2014 CheckIdempotencyKey** *(ungoverned \u2014 no transaction yet)*\n- [side-effect] Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header and publishes it downstream.\n- [validation/short-circuit] If that key was already recorded, throws `IdempotentReplayException` carrying the previously created owner \u2192 replays it with **200**, no write.\n\n*(Transaction opens here; every step from `build` on is `govern: [ transaction ]`, committing once at the end.)*\n\n**2. `build` \u2014 BuildOwner** \u2014 binds `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`, so **bean validation runs here** (any failure \u2192 **400**):\n- `firstName`: `@NotNull`, pattern `^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$`, size 1\u201330\n- `lastName`: `@NotNull`, pattern `\u2026\\.?$`, size 1\u201330\n- `title`: size \u2264 10\n- `address`: non-blank pattern, size 1\u2013255 (optional)\n- `addressLine1` / `addressLine2`: size \u2264 255\n- `city`: `@NotNull`, non-blank, size 1\u201380\n- `telephone`: `@NotNull`, size 1\u201320\n- `email`: size \u2264 255\n- `postcode`: pattern `^[0-9]{4}$`\n- [side-effect] Maps the DTO to a new `Owner` entity and republishes both the entity and the request DTO.\n\n**3. `rejectFutureRegistrationDate`** \u2014 [validation] if a `registrationDate` was supplied and is after today \u2192 **400** (checked before any defaulting).\n\n**4. `defaultRegistrationDate`** \u2014 [side-effect] defaults `registrationDate` to today if absent, then rolls a Saturday/Sunday/listed-public-holiday date forward to the next business day. Later date-derived values see this adjusted date.\n\n**5. `normalize` \u2014 NormalizeOwnerTelephone** \u2014 [validation] telephone must form valid E.164 (else **400**); [side-effect] rewrites it to canonical E.164 (e.g. `0412 345 678` \u2192 `+61412345678`).\n\n**6. `normalizeEmail`** \u2014 optional; if present, [validation] must be syntactically valid (else **400**); [side-effect] lower-cases it.\n\n**7. `rejectDisposableEmailDomain`** \u2014 [validation] if the (now normalized) email's domain is on the disposable blocklist \u2192 **400**.\n\n**8. `normalizeAddress`** \u2014 [side-effect] normalizes address (trim/collapse/upper-case, expand street abbreviations); prefers structured `addressLine1`(+`addressLine2`) and composes the flat `address` from them, else normalizes the flat `address`. [validation] must have a non-blank `addressLine1` **or** flat `address` (else **400**).\n\n**9. `rejectInvalidPostcode`** \u2014 [validation] if a postcode is present, it must fall in the range for the region derived from the city (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown city accepts any 4-digit) \u2192 **400** if out of range.\n\n**10. `assignHousehold`** \u2014 [side-effect] derives `householdId` = first 12 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `regionCodeV2|normalizedLastName|postcode`; left null when last name or postcode is missing.\n\n**11. `rejectDuplicateIdentity`** \u2014 [validation] rejects (**409**) only on an exact `identityKey` match (SHA-256 over normalizedTelephone|lowerEmail|soundex(lastName)) against an existing **non-deleted** owner. Soft-deleted owners are skipped.\n\n**12. `rejectCityCapacity`** \u2014 [validation] if the owner's (normalized) city already holds \u2265 50 owners \u2192 **409**.\n\n**13. `rejectDailyLimit`** \u2014 [validation] if \u2265 100 owners already share this owner's business-day `registrationDate` \u2192 **429**.\n\n**14. `assignPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 [side-effect] sets `possibleDuplicateOf` to the earliest existing owner whose `soundex(lastName)` and `postcode` match but whose identityKey differs. Skipped entirely when `sharesHousehold` is true, or last name/postcode missing.\n\n**15. `assignHouseholdSize`** \u2014 [side-effect] sets `householdSize` = existing members sharing `householdId` + 1 (1 when no household).\n\n**16. `capMembershipLevel`** \u2014 [side-effect] sets `membershipLevelCap` to one above the max membership level among existing household members (left null when no existing member).\n\n**17. `assignMemberId`** \u2014 [side-effect] computes `memberId` = `<REGION><FY><HASH8><Luhn-check>`; de-duplicates against existing memberIds by appending `-<n>`.\n\n**18. `assignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 [side-effect] sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n**19. `assignBulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 [side-effect] sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true when > 80 owners already share the business day.\n\n**20. `assignCapacityWarning`** \u2014 [side-effect] sets `capacityWarning` = true when the city holds 40\u201349 other owners.\n\n**21. `save` \u2014 SaveOwner** \u2014 [side-effect] persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (the write, inside the transaction).\n\n**22. `audit` \u2014 AuditOwnerCreated** \u2014 [side-effect] emits an `AUDIT` human-readable line plus a structured schema-v2 JSON `OWNER_CREATED` event, incrementing a process-wide sequence counter.\n\n**23. `enqueueWelcome`** \u2014 [side-effect] emits a `NOTIFY` line carrying the owner id and memberId.\n\n**24. `recordIdempotency`** \u2014 [side-effect] if an `Idempotency-Key` was supplied, stores the response DTO against it so a later same-key create replays instead of duplicating.\n\n**25. `respond` \u2014 RespondWithOwnerCreated** \u2014 [side-effect] maps to `OwnerDto` and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Notes\n- Ordering is deliberate: validation-that-rejects steps (2\u20133, 5\u20137, 9, 11\u201313) are interleaved with mutating steps so that, e.g., a future date is caught before defaulting, and body validation (400) precedes the not-found/duplicate/capacity checks.\n- Everything from step 2 onward runs in a **single transaction** that commits once after step 24; step 1 is intentionally left ungoverned so an idempotent replay opens no transaction.\n\nI didn't change anything \u2014 this is a read-only trace."
